# Loading UI

- **Always** use the shared loading components from `components/common` for any loading / pending UI.
- Asset: `src/assets/live-chatbot.svg` (do not swap in random spinners, CSS dots, or third-party loaders).

## Components

| Use case | Component |
|----------|-----------|
| Inline / button / small area | `<Loading size="sm" />` or `size="md"` |
| Page / section / full viewport | `<LoadingScreen />` (optional `label`) |
| Overlay over existing content | `<LoadingOverlay />` |

## Rules

- Do **not** invent one-off loaders (`animate-spin`, Lucide `Loader2`, browser `busy` text alone).
- Buttons that wait on async work should show `<Loading size="sm" />` (or disable + nearby loader) via the shared component.
- Feature pages awaiting data must render `LoadingScreen` (or `Loading` inside the content area), not blank screens or custom spinners.
- Keep the chatbot SVG as the only loading visual language in the app.

If the user asks for a different spinner, redirect to these components unless they explicitly override.
